+# Proposal 0008: `color.bg.brand-secondary` and `color.bg.brand-secondary-hover` (Primary_alt button)
+
+- **Status:** ✅ Approved with conditions and merged (2026-11-10). All conditions verified below
+- **Files:** `tokens/themes/light/color.tokens.json`, `tokens/themes/dark/color.tokens.json`. 2 entries added to `color.bg` in each, after `brand-primary-hover`. No other key, value, alias or type changes.
+
+## Why
+
+Button `Hierarchy=Primary_alt` is the secondary-brand (lime) button used in the login flow. Task C1 (2026-11-09) rebound its fills from the primitive `Colors/Green lime/500` to the existing Figma semantic variables below. The registry had no matching role, so code could only use the primitive.
+
+## Tokens
+
+| Token | Light | Dark | Figma variable (unchanged) | Tailwind (option A roles) | Use |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `color.bg.brand-secondary` | `{color.green-lime.500}` #d0ff00 | same | `Colors/Background/bg-brand-secondary` `VariableID:5363:390066` | `bg-brand-secondary` | Primary_alt Default, Focused, Loading, Disabled base (21 fills) |
+| `color.bg.brand-secondary-hover` | `{color.green-lime.400}` #d9ff75 | same | `Colors/Background/bg-brand-secondary_hover` `VariableID:17490:23029` | `bg-brand-secondary-hover` | Primary_alt Hover and Pressed (14 fills) |
+
+- Text on these backgrounds: black (`Colors/Text/text-primary_on-brandsecondary`, not in the registry yet).
+- Dark = Light: dark mode is flat in the pilot (ADR-0007).
+
+## Condition checks (2026-11-10)
+
+| Condition | Result | Evidence (make-ds2-workspace) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Both exist as Figma semantic variables | ✅ `1. Color modes`, scopes `FRAME_FILL` + `SHAPE_FILL`, published | `reports/auth-readiness/figma-brand-secondary.json` |
+| Light/Dark values and aliases preserved | ✅ Each registry alias equals the Figma alias in both modes. Sync dry-run: 4 rows `unchanged` (matched by `figmaVariableId`), 0 create / update / conflict, so no Figma write is needed | `reports/auth-readiness/dryrun/` |
+| No duplicate of an existing token with the same role | ✅ No `color.bg.*` or other registry token resolves to #d0ff00 / #d9ff75. In Figma the same values are also used by `focus-ring-alt` and `bg-avatar-color1`, which are different roles and not in the registry. Note: Figma `text-brand-secondary` / `fg-brand-secondary` are **blue** (Brand 500–800); names are compared only within a namespace (convention §10), so this is not a duplicate | same JSON |
+| Intended use documented | ✅ `$description` + this proposal | — |
+| Tailwind / NativeWind compatible | ✅ **Tailwind 4.3.5** compile (workspace `compile-check.mjs` S6, 69/69): `bg-brand-secondary` → `background-color: var(--background-color-brand-secondary)`, `-hover` and `hover:` likewise; `bg-brand-primary`, `bg-brand-primary-hover`, `text-brand-primary`, `bg-gray-100` and `p-3` identical to S1; no `--color-*` key emitted. Tailwind's own `lime` palette does not collide (registry primitive is `green-lime`, kept in `:root`). **NativeWind:** static check only, not compiled: the same class names, the values are static sRGB hex, and there is no key collision with the Tailwind v3 default palette | `reports/token-naming/compile-check/` |
+| Existing tokens and appearance unchanged | ✅ `dist/` (`build:paper-kit`): only the 2 tokens added per mode (+12 resolved entries each), 0 removed / changed; `paper-kit/kit.json` identical. No Figma change (bindings were already in place since C1) | — |
+
+## Validation
+
+- `npm run check`: ✔ themes 11 → 13 per mode (primitives 120, semantic 8 unchanged); tests 29/29.
+
+## Approval
+
+Mike, 2026-11-10: "MAKE DS2 — Authentication Component Final Readiness … 2. Primary_alt semantic tokens — CONDITIONALLY APPROVED. Add `color.bg.brand-secondary` and `color.bg.brand-secondary-hover` to the canonical `design-tokens` registry after verifying" the conditions above.
